  "summary": "This experiment tested a single-modality RNA-only model (config_001) without image data or fusion, achieving validation accuracy of 0.4849 and F1 of 0.4639. These results suggest the RNA-only approach underperforms compared to the multimodal baseline (config_016) with validation accuracy 0.5266. The effectiveness of alternative single-modality configurations and RNA encoder choices remains uncertain without direct comparisons."
